{
  "rationale": "The plant automaton G1 models the robot's local perception and motion capabilities, including all controllable and uncontrollable events. The specification automata E1-E4 encode the safe and coverage-biased exploration policy: E1 binds clear perception to forward/random_walk actions, E2 enforces conservative obstacle recovery, E3 prevents repeated backward actions, and E4 ensures the robot returns to exploration after recovery. The design ensures safety by always passing through a recovery state after obstacle events, uses move_backward only for front-obstacle recovery, and prioritizes forward progress and coverage in clear states.",
  "strategy": [
    "Model robot perception and motion as a single plant automaton with all required events and helper states for commit/recovery.",
    "Use layered specifications to enforce safe obstacle recovery, prevent repeated backward actions, and bias toward forward exploration and coverage."
  ],
